{
  "schema": "marfagenez.experiment-result.v2",
  "name": "exp25_crowding_law",
  "question": "Does k_max = 1 + floor((M*r - maintenance - damage)/income) hold on parameters that did not take part in deriving it?",
  "arithmetic": {
    "law": "k_max = 1 + floor((M*r - maintenance - damage_rate)/income)",
    "jump_r": "r = (income + maintenance + damage_rate)/M",
    "derivation": "life.rs:429-441 draws for every organism, then regrow_all() once, so on one cell the draws are sequential with no regrowth between them. The cell is drained to zero and regrows to M*r, so the step starts at c = M*r and the k-th organism gets min(income, M*r - (k-1)*income). organism.rs:148-182 gives the per-step ledger net = taken - maintenance_cost - damage_rate, so a survivor needs taken >= maintenance_cost + damage_rate.",
    "first_version_was_wrong": "The first version omitted damage_rate and treated maintenance as a minimum share rather than a fixed per-step cost. It also assumed maintenance could be varied freely; with income = 0.8 and damage_rate = 0.02 any maintenance >= 0.78 kills everyone, because taken is capped at income.",
    "saturation": "n = 320 = 8 x 40 cells, so every cell starts crowded",
    "damage_rate": 0.02,
    "predicted_k_max": [
      1,
      1,
      2,
      2,
      2,
      2,
      2,
      2,
      2,
      2
    ]
  },
